            "review_title": "Review at Bi Coffee",
            "review_text": "Jacob G\nCollege Station, Texas112 contributions\n0\nThe Skinny!\nSep 2018 • Couples\nLet me give you the SKINNY on this unassuming place. So, 1) there are a lot of drink options - coffee, juices, smoothies... whatever you want. That is all fine and dandy, but 2) not to somehow hint this as a negative thing -- quite the opposite, actually -- but they serve only one type of food here, and it is done oh so superbly: \"Bánh canh vịt\" - it is a type of chicken noodle soup... and in a few variations you can choose from. Let me just lay it down on the table: they make the noodles in house! I'll let that sink in. [looks at watch]... anyone in the know knows that making any RICE based noodle is difficult and unforgiving! And they do this rare type of noodle well!!! Thick short noodles. Imagine \"chicken & dumplings\" and you are on the right track. Their soup almost tastes identical to this American classic... and the noodles are the same texture as the classic flat \"dumpling\" (not the balls). The soup is mmmmm mmm good! So if you are in Vietnam, and you are within 10 minutes, and you have a hankering for breakfast, brunch, lunch or dinner, it is worth giving their \"bánh canh vịt\" a try!\nRead more\nWritten October 2, 2018",
